 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.06666666666666667,
   "dur": 3.734,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "Same list as cigarettes? Processed meat is on it too."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 4.966666666666667,
   "dur": 10.406,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "All three share the top group of the World Health Organization's cancer agency, which says that doesn't make them equally dangerous: it ranks how sure the evidence is."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 16.166666666666668,
   "dur": 11.758,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "Into the bed, then: its light is mostly UVA, the long rays. In large, powerful units, it may be ten to fifteen times as intense as the midday sun."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 28.766666666666666,
   "dur": 10.784,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "When the beds joined that group, the sharpest signal came from people who started young. In pooled studies, first use before thirty-five went with melanoma risk raised by more than half."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 42.3,
   "dur": 6.191,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "Whole countries acted: Australia switched off every commercial bed in the land, and Brazil banned them too."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 52.1,
   "dur": 6.391,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "And those long rays reach right through the top layer, on most skin about as thin as paper."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 59.1,
   "dur": 8.096,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "The sun made that list years before the beds. Same list as cigarettes: not the same harm, the same certainty."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "t": 67.96666666666667,
   "dur": 3.922,
   "file": "vo/08.wav",
   "text": "Next season: why do bath fingers wrinkle, but never your arm?"
  }
 ]
